WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:01.620
- Thanks to CuriosityStream

00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:03.210
for keeping LegalEagle in the air.

00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:04.650
By clicking the link in the description,

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:06.330
you'll also get Nebula for free,

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:10.136
a streaming platform made
by and for creators like me.

00:00:10.136 --> 00:00:11.810
(gentle music)

00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:14.430
The time is the roaring '20s.

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:18.460
The place, the glamorous
downtown streets of Chicago.

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:21.170
Gangsters and bootleggers
capture most of the headlines

00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:22.910
and the attention of police.

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:25.290
Clubs overflow with the
young, the beautiful,

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:26.560
and the rebellious.

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:29.230
There's too much jazz
and never enough gin.

00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:32.590
But then a strange and horrible event

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:35.280
shakes the city from its euphoria.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:39.660
In fact, the whole world is
rocked by a deadly crime spree

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:41.410
pulled off by two of the wealthiest

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:44.220
and most promising young men in the city.

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:48.570
A pair of rich geniuses
brutally murder a boy

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:50.940
for their own callous amusement

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:53.440
and intellectual curiosity.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:57.870
The victim, Bobby Franks, only age 14.

00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:01.140
News that an innocent boy
has been killed in cold blood

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:03.340
as part of a twisted experiment

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:06.600
sweeps across the country like wildfire.

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:08.720
America speculates in a frenzy.

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:11.180
What could've driven
these two rich gentlemen

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:13.550
to murder for fun?

00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:17.280
Plagued by a dark psychosis
that no one detected,

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:19.830
the young scholars, prodigies,

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:23.120
arrogantly explained their heartless plan.

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:27.310
The killers, Nathan
Leopold and Richard Loeb.

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:29.980
Does anyone who kills
for a twisted ideology

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:32.080
have grounds for anything less

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:34.330
than the harshest sentence?

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:37.027
That's the question
that we have to face in

00:01:37.027 --> 00:01:41.287
"The Case of Leopold and
Loeb: The Genius Murderers."

00:01:44.510 --> 00:01:46.400
We present for your adjudication

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:51.690
young Nathan Leopold, age
19, undeniably a genius.

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:54.990
His IQ is in the top 2% of
those tested at this time.

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:57.500
Though he didn't speak his
first word until age four,

00:01:57.500 --> 00:01:59.500
he now speaks 15 languages,

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:02.010
and he has just graduated
from the University of Chicago

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:03.740
with Phi Beta Kappa honors.

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:06.030
He's charming, the envy of younger boys

00:02:06.030 --> 00:02:09.010
and suitor to a stunning young
woman of impeccable breeding.

00:02:09.010 --> 00:02:10.840
Leopold is dashing and brilliant.

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:13.400
He believes the world
is his for the taking.

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:15.510
And his accomplish, Richard Loeb,

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:17.920
age 18, another prodigy.

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:19.570
After becoming the youngest graduate

00:02:19.570 --> 00:02:22.310
from the University of
Michigan at the age of 17,

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:24.520
Loeb is currently working
on his graduate studies

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:26.190
at the University of Chicago.

00:02:26.190 --> 00:02:28.270
Despite his impressive school record,

00:02:28.270 --> 00:02:31.410
Loeb is not excited by
intellectual pursuits.

00:02:31.410 --> 00:02:34.690
He'd rather be playing tennis
or reading detective stories.

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:36.200
Like most teenage boys,

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:39.720
Loeb loves the puzzle-solving
challenge of crime novels,

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:40.940
so reads a lot of books

00:02:40.940 --> 00:02:44.440
in which the bad guy always get caught.

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:48.060
These two rising stars
collide in the early 1920s.

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:50.680
Although Leopold and Loeb
know each other as children,

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:52.440
they become close during their time

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:53.740
at the University of Chicago

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:56.120
where their genius
intellect set them apart

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:57.880
from the rest of the student body.

00:02:57.880 --> 00:03:00.620
They decide to find their
own interest and ventures.

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:04.090
Ones that appealed to their
inflated sense of self-worth.

00:03:04.090 --> 00:03:06.440
Leopold and Loeb have
separately been lauded

00:03:06.440 --> 00:03:08.750
as prodigies since they were toddlers.

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:10.030
Together, they come to believe

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:13.280
that they are truly superior
to nearly everyone else,

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:16.450
in fact, 99% of society.

00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:19.420
So when they read the works of
German philosopher Nietzsche,

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:22.130
they seize upon his idea of the superman,

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:24.320
a transcendent individual who posses

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:27.300
extraordinary and unusual capabilities,

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:29.230
which makes them above the laws

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:31.700
that bind normal society.

00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:34.040
This philosophy further warps the minds

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:36.170
of our two young scholars.

00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:37.940
Leopold, entranced by the idea

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:39.820
that he and Loeb are so extraordinary

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:41.600
that different rules apply to them,

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:44.310
urges his friend to
adopt the same beliefs,

00:03:44.310 --> 00:03:46.617
writing, "A superman is on account of

00:03:46.617 --> 00:03:49.357
"certain superior
qualities inherent in him,

00:03:49.357 --> 00:03:52.217
"exempted from the ordinary
laws which govern men.

00:03:52.217 --> 00:03:55.510
"He's not liable for anything he may do."

00:03:55.510 --> 00:03:57.600
Loeb needs little convincing.

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:00.911
The duo sets out to
commit a string of crimes

00:04:00.911 --> 00:04:01.744
(fire crackling)

00:04:01.744 --> 00:04:02.624
and they get away

00:04:02.624 --> 00:04:03.600
(glass shatters)

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:04.940
with all of them.

00:04:04.940 --> 00:04:06.390
But the criminal scholars decide

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:09.610
to push this Nietzschean
theory even further.

00:04:09.610 --> 00:04:12.750
They resolve to aim higher,
not arson or battery.

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:15.853
No, this time, they plan a murder.

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:19.100
One so cold and callous,

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:20.510
it will become one of the most red

00:04:20.510 --> 00:04:23.510
and studied legal cases of all time.

00:04:23.510 --> 00:04:28.380
In short, they set out to
commit the perfect crime,

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:31.570
one that is, the
psychotic buddies believe,

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:34.800
they can pull of with complete immunity.

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:37.410
In 1929, Leopold and Loeb begin

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:39.510
preparations for the killing,

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:42.390
a plan that begins with
the already heinous crime

00:04:42.390 --> 00:04:43.900
of kidnapping.

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:46.900
Because the two resolve to
murder an innocent child,

00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:50.480
they first must decide how
the abduction will take place.

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:52.200
Should they take the boy from his bedroom

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:53.440
in the middle of the night,

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:55.160
perhaps steal him away from his family

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:56.750
while they're out on the town?

00:04:56.750 --> 00:04:59.197
They then begin contemplating
the murder itself.

00:04:59.197 --> 00:05:01.067
"How should we kill him?" they asked.

00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:02.227
"Poison,

00:05:02.227 --> 00:05:03.063
"shooting,

00:05:04.017 --> 00:05:05.630
"stabbing?"

00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:09.550
They coldly discussed one
gruesome idea after another

00:05:09.550 --> 00:05:12.430
before at last settling on a method.

00:05:12.430 --> 00:05:13.740
For these evil geniuses,

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:16.440
there are still more preparations to make.

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:18.260
Another part of their diabolical plan

00:05:18.260 --> 00:05:20.730
involves typing a ransom
note from a fake person

00:05:20.730 --> 00:05:23.070
and creating a bank
account in a false name

00:05:23.070 --> 00:05:24.480
into which the victim's family

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:26.204
can deposit the ransom money.

00:05:26.204 --> 00:05:27.200
(cash register rings)

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:29.420
Dispassionately, they
discuss renting a car

00:05:29.420 --> 00:05:32.100
and typing the ransom
demand on a typewriter

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:35.090
that Loeb steals from
his own fraternity house.

00:05:35.090 --> 00:05:38.120
The pair plot and complete
each villainous step,

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:40.000
seemingly failing to realize

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:43.490
that each one exposes
them to more eyewitnesses.

00:05:43.490 --> 00:05:45.950
The two demented prodigy
spend seven months

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:47.830
making their murderous plans.

00:05:47.830 --> 00:05:51.090
At last, on May 21st, 1924,

00:05:51.090 --> 00:05:53.520
on a warm and cloudless spring day,

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:56.710
Leopold and Loeb put their
long-plotted gruesome plan

00:05:56.710 --> 00:05:57.930
into action.

00:05:57.930 --> 00:06:00.360
First, they lured
14-year-old Bobby Franks,

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:02.680
a trusty neighbor, tennis buddy,

00:06:02.680 --> 00:06:05.523
and second cousin of
Loeb's, to the rental car.

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:09.320
The charming killers whom
Bobby knows and looks up to

00:06:09.320 --> 00:06:10.980
convinced him to come to their car

00:06:10.980 --> 00:06:12.360
to discuss a new tennis racket

00:06:12.360 --> 00:06:13.800
that Loeb as been using.

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:17.973
They then seize him,
bind him, and speed away.

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:21.533
The kidnapping has begun.

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:24.760
After the madmen have Bobby in the car,

00:06:24.760 --> 00:06:27.070
the horrific deed moves into full swing.

00:06:27.070 --> 00:06:28.160
As Leopold drives,

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:31.220
Loeb repeatedly hits Bobby in
the head with a metal chisel,

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:32.540
then drags him into the backseat

00:06:32.540 --> 00:06:35.430
where the dreadful undertaking continues.

00:06:35.430 --> 00:06:39.010
In the backseat, Loeb gags
young Bobby with his own hands,

00:06:39.010 --> 00:06:40.930
covering Bobby's nose and face,

00:06:40.930 --> 00:06:43.420
until the ill-fated child
can no longer breathe

00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:46.400
and at last suffocates.

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:49.190
Now, traveling with their victim's body,

00:06:49.190 --> 00:06:50.780
the depraved men drive on

00:06:50.780 --> 00:06:52.810
to their predetermined dumping site,

00:06:52.810 --> 00:06:55.940
25 miles south of Chicago in Indiana.

00:06:55.940 --> 00:07:00.290
For the entire trip, Bobby
lies hidden beneath the robe.

00:07:00.290 --> 00:07:03.740
The brutal murder has no
effect on these two monsters.

00:07:03.740 --> 00:07:05.360
In fact, they grab a bite to eat

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:08.240
on their way to dispose
of the poor boy's remains.

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:10.210
Shockingly, they even eat in the car

00:07:10.210 --> 00:07:12.490
with the corpse as they drive along.

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:15.520
After sundown, they heartlessly
strip Bobby of his clothes

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:17.580
and drag his lifeless body to a culvert

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:19.180
near some railroad tracks.

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:20.160
Loeb keeps a look out

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:23.470
while Leopold carefully
removes his own coat and shoes,

00:07:23.470 --> 00:07:24.810
and then dawns a pair of boots

00:07:24.810 --> 00:07:27.070
to take the remains into the sewer canal.

00:07:27.070 --> 00:07:29.060
To try to prevent Bobby's identification,

00:07:29.060 --> 00:07:32.570
in a grizzly act, Leopold
pours hydrochloric acid

00:07:32.570 --> 00:07:34.350
on his face and body.

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:37.040
Finally, he covers Bobby
with a robe once more.

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:38.830
Leopold emerges from the tunnel,

00:07:38.830 --> 00:07:41.570
confident that his work
has been meticulous.

00:07:41.570 --> 00:07:43.940
But unbeknownst to either of the killers,

00:07:43.940 --> 00:07:46.780
Leopold's glasses are
left at the dumping site.

00:07:46.780 --> 00:07:48.560
their twisted sense of superiority

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:50.150
prevents them from ever considering

00:07:50.150 --> 00:07:52.300
the possibility of human error.

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:55.640
Feeling secure in their
grizzly endeavor so far,

00:07:55.640 --> 00:07:58.040
they duck back into their
blood-stained rental car

00:07:58.040 --> 00:08:00.170
and head back to Chicago.

00:08:00.170 --> 00:08:02.030
But unnoticed by the murders,

00:08:02.030 --> 00:08:04.560
eyewitnesses continue to accumulate.

00:08:04.560 --> 00:08:05.910
On their drive back north,

00:08:05.910 --> 00:08:07.050
a woman and her daughter

00:08:07.050 --> 00:08:09.160
are on their way home from a picture show.

00:08:09.160 --> 00:08:10.150
Since the road is dark,

00:08:10.150 --> 00:08:11.390
the mother flashes her brights

00:08:11.390 --> 00:08:13.060
when approaching Leopold's and Loeb's car

00:08:13.060 --> 00:08:14.640
coming from the other direction.

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:18.260
The ladies get a clear look
at the car passing them.

00:08:18.260 --> 00:08:20.460
It's around 9:30 p.m.

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:22.460
Next, Leopold stops at a drugstore

00:08:22.460 --> 00:08:23.970
to call his girlfriend in his home,

00:08:23.970 --> 00:08:25.280
claiming that he's still nearby

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:26.470
and out with friends.

00:08:26.470 --> 00:08:28.327
He tells them he'll be a
little later getting back.

00:08:28.327 --> 00:08:30.400
And in turn, his parents remind him

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:33.030
that he must drive his
aunt home upon his return.

00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:34.690
Leopold hopes these conversations

00:08:34.690 --> 00:08:35.700
will support an alibi.

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:39.240
But of course, phone
calls are no such proof.

00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:40.580
Finally, back in Chicago,

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:43.660
the nefarious pair begin
to dispose of the evidence.

00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:44.780
They stop at Loeb's home

00:08:44.780 --> 00:08:47.770
where Loeb burns BObby's
clothes in the furnace.

00:08:47.770 --> 00:08:48.840
Meanwhile in the garage,

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:49.910
Leopold attempts to clean

00:08:49.910 --> 00:08:52.830
Bobby's bloodstain from the
rental car's front seat.

00:08:52.830 --> 00:08:54.330
Thinking the large robe may cause

00:08:54.330 --> 00:08:55.620
too much some in the furnace,

00:08:55.620 --> 00:08:57.140
the two decided to hide in the yard

00:08:57.140 --> 00:08:58.950
and plan to burn it later.

00:08:58.950 --> 00:09:01.400
Still feeling pleased with
the execution of their plan,

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:03.880
Loeb stays with Leopold's
family at their house

00:09:03.880 --> 00:09:07.250
while Leopold at last
drives his aunt home,

00:09:07.250 --> 00:09:09.330
but their terrible business
on this faithful night

00:09:09.330 --> 00:09:11.200
is not done yet.

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:14.010
At around 10:30 p.m.
before returning home,

00:09:14.010 --> 00:09:15.480
Leopold calls Bobby's parents,

00:09:15.480 --> 00:09:17.662
pretending to be the man
named George Johnson.

00:09:17.662 --> 00:09:18.495
(phone ringing)

00:09:18.495 --> 00:09:19.630
Bobby's unsuspecting mother

00:09:19.630 --> 00:09:21.220
answers the call and receives news

00:09:21.220 --> 00:09:24.510
that throws her life
into a living nightmare.

00:09:24.510 --> 00:09:26.460
Lying, Leopold tells Mrs. Franks

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:29.750
that her son, Bobby, has been
kidnapped but is unharmed.

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:31.240
And he ordered Mrs. Franks to wait

00:09:31.240 --> 00:09:34.630
for further instructions
regarding the $10,000 ransom.

00:09:34.630 --> 00:09:36.370
He warns her that she and her husband

00:09:36.370 --> 00:09:37.930
must strictly follow his directions,

00:09:37.930 --> 00:09:40.800
and that they cannot contact the police.

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:42.310
Once Leopold arrives home,

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:44.110
he and Loeb settled down to wait

00:09:44.110 --> 00:09:45.493
and play cards for a while.

00:09:46.420 --> 00:09:47.770
Around one o'clock in the morning,

00:09:47.770 --> 00:09:49.310
the two leave in the rental car

00:09:49.310 --> 00:09:50.610
to mail their ransom note,

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:53.330
dropping it off for special
delivery to the Franks.

00:09:53.330 --> 00:09:54.960
On the way back to Loeb's house,

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:58.490
Loeb tosses the chisel into
some brush along the roadside.

00:09:58.490 --> 00:10:01.230
Leopold drops off Loeb at around 1:40 a.m.

00:10:01.230 --> 00:10:04.970
and heads back home as their
bloody crimes draw to a close,

00:10:04.970 --> 00:10:06.960
but the Franks' nightmare
is far from over.

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:09.790
The next day, the ransom
demand arrives around noon,

00:10:09.790 --> 00:10:11.460
which Mrs. Franks can barely open

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:14.240
because her hands are shaking so badly.

00:10:14.240 --> 00:10:16.080
Desperately, the Franks try to understand

00:10:16.080 --> 00:10:17.610
the letter's instructions.

00:10:17.610 --> 00:10:18.930
They must wait at their home

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:21.410
for another call at one o'clock p.m.,

00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:23.830
which will tell them
where to leave the money.

00:10:23.830 --> 00:10:27.177
The letter is signed George
Johnson, and concludes,

00:10:27.177 --> 00:10:29.297
"Remember that this is your only chance

00:10:29.297 --> 00:10:31.600
"to recovery your son."

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:32.790
But at the very moments,

00:10:32.790 --> 00:10:34.410
the police are already unraveling

00:10:34.410 --> 00:10:37.240
Leopold and Loeb's, quote, perfect crime.

00:10:37.240 --> 00:10:39.490
Their first mistake, the chisel that Loeb

00:10:39.490 --> 00:10:41.160
threw out into the brush.

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:42.660
A man who is watching curiously

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:44.640
decided to see what had been tossed

00:10:44.640 --> 00:10:46.669
from the window of their fancy rental car

00:10:46.669 --> 00:10:47.502
in the middle of the night.

00:10:47.502 --> 00:10:48.335
(gasps)

00:10:48.335 --> 00:10:49.880
He was shocked to find the bloody chisel.

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:52.300
And by 2:30 a.m., that eyewitness

00:10:52.300 --> 00:10:54.890
has turned the murder
weapon over to police.

00:10:54.890 --> 00:10:56.480
The two self-proclaimed geniuses

00:10:56.480 --> 00:10:58.940
having an inkling that
tangible evidence against them

00:10:58.940 --> 00:11:00.910
is already being collected.

00:11:00.910 --> 00:11:03.510
Mere hours later, two
early morning workmen

00:11:03.510 --> 00:11:06.160
happen to cross Bobby's remains

00:11:06.160 --> 00:11:10.080
where they also find Leopold's spectacles.

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:12.500
They gently removed the
boy's body from the culvert

00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:14.060
and contact police.

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:15.970
When the police arrived, they also find

00:11:15.970 --> 00:11:17.770
one of Bobby Frank's socks.

00:11:17.770 --> 00:11:19.680
By late morning, Leopold and Loeb

00:11:19.680 --> 00:11:22.120
are scrubbing the carpet
in the rear of the car.

00:11:22.120 --> 00:11:24.000
Leopold's chauffeur happens upon them

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:26.420
and Leopold clumsily invents a story.

00:11:26.420 --> 00:11:28.250
They spilled some red wine in the car,

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:31.030
and they're cleaning it out
so Loeb's father won't see it.

00:11:31.030 --> 00:11:35.100
This might make sense, but
this is not Loeb's car.

00:11:35.100 --> 00:11:37.490
At 2:00 p.m., an hour after the Franks

00:11:37.490 --> 00:11:39.330
expect more instructions,

00:11:39.330 --> 00:11:41.700
Leopold drops off Loeb
at the train station

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:43.500
where Loeb buys a train ticket

00:11:43.500 --> 00:11:45.420
in his own name for Michigan City.

00:11:45.420 --> 00:11:47.530
He quickly boards the
car and deposits a letter

00:11:47.530 --> 00:11:49.370
in the train's telegraph rack.

00:11:49.370 --> 00:11:51.380
The criminal masterminds
hope to trick authorities

00:11:51.380 --> 00:11:53.060
into believing that Loeb was on the train

00:11:53.060 --> 00:11:54.260
at the very time the franks

00:11:54.260 --> 00:11:56.313
are due to be contacted in Chicago.

00:11:57.290 --> 00:12:00.170
Meanwhile, Leopold doesn't waste any time.

00:12:00.170 --> 00:12:02.410
While Loeb is planting
the letters on the train,

00:12:02.410 --> 00:12:04.780
Leopold goes to a drugstore
and calls the Franks,

00:12:04.780 --> 00:12:06.950
instructing them to go
to a different drugstore

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:09.060
and wait there for another call.

00:12:09.060 --> 00:12:10.170
Leopold gives the Franks

00:12:10.170 --> 00:12:11.850
the designated address and hangs up,

00:12:11.850 --> 00:12:14.720
then hurries back to pick up
Loeb from the train station.

00:12:14.720 --> 00:12:17.120
Once together again,
the naive perpetrators

00:12:17.120 --> 00:12:18.910
go back to the drugstore near the station

00:12:18.910 --> 00:12:20.600
to call the other drugstore

00:12:20.600 --> 00:12:23.390
where they believe the
Franks are anxiously waiting.

00:12:23.390 --> 00:12:25.490
But by now, Bobby's body has already been

00:12:25.490 --> 00:12:28.610
identified by his uncle and
is in the county morgue.

00:12:28.610 --> 00:12:30.240
Remarkably, just five minutes

00:12:30.240 --> 00:12:32.110
before Leopold called the Franks,

00:12:32.110 --> 00:12:33.430
the police arrived to give them

00:12:33.430 --> 00:12:34.640
the life-shattering news

00:12:34.640 --> 00:12:36.840
that their poor little boy is dead.

00:12:36.840 --> 00:12:38.820
Of course, the Franks are not going

00:12:38.820 --> 00:12:41.027
to any drugstore at this point.

00:12:41.027 --> 00:12:42.320
Before the day is out,

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:44.350
much to the deranged managed to grin,

00:12:44.350 --> 00:12:46.950
Bobby's death is already
in the newspapers.

00:12:46.950 --> 00:12:50.160
With Bobby dead, how can they
pull off a ransom payday now?

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:52.170
In a panic, Loeb urges Leopold

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:53.630
to call everything off,

00:12:53.630 --> 00:12:55.480
but Leopold stubbornly disagrees,

00:12:55.480 --> 00:12:58.920
racking his brilliant mind for
a way to still get the money.

00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:01.520
But failing to come up with
anything, Leopold agrees.

00:13:01.520 --> 00:13:03.250
The new plan is to plan evidence

00:13:03.250 --> 00:13:05.730
to make it look like
someone else murdered Bobby.

00:13:05.730 --> 00:13:07.650
Once the two get rid of their rental car,

00:13:07.650 --> 00:13:11.200
they decide to try to pin the
murder on one George Lewis,

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:12.540
an ornithology student

00:13:12.540 --> 00:13:15.560
in one of the zoology
classes Leopold teaches.

00:13:15.560 --> 00:13:17.640
Leopold's genius idea is to frame

00:13:17.640 --> 00:13:19.400
one of his bird enthusiast students,

00:13:19.400 --> 00:13:21.980
because some of them
frequent the part of Indiana

00:13:21.980 --> 00:13:23.850
where Bobby's remains were found.

00:13:23.850 --> 00:13:25.360
Leopold doesn't even consider

00:13:25.360 --> 00:13:28.140
that Lewis may have a rock-solid alibi.

00:13:28.140 --> 00:13:31.538
How could two geniuses be so birdbrained?

00:13:31.538 --> 00:13:32.420
(bird screeching)

00:13:32.420 --> 00:13:34.350
The two were acting in a blind panic now.

00:13:34.350 --> 00:13:36.270
Their smug intelligence proving

00:13:36.270 --> 00:13:38.640
the crumbling facade as the net closes in.

00:13:38.640 --> 00:13:40.990
Driving with no consideration
for the speed limit,

00:13:40.990 --> 00:13:42.520
Leopold picks up Loeb.

00:13:42.520 --> 00:13:44.480
They retrieved Bobby's
robe from the backyard

00:13:44.480 --> 00:13:46.070
and drive to a secluded spot.

00:13:46.070 --> 00:13:47.610
They burned it on the side of the road,

00:13:47.610 --> 00:13:49.540
out of anyone's sight,
as far as they know.

00:13:49.540 --> 00:13:51.410
They then speed to Indiana where they hide

00:13:51.410 --> 00:13:54.200
Bobby's class pin, belt buckle, and shoes.

00:13:54.200 --> 00:13:56.410
But before they can finish
their cover-up plan,

00:13:56.410 --> 00:13:58.760
Captain Wolfe of the
Chicago Police Department

00:13:58.760 --> 00:14:01.080
calls Leopold in for questioning.

00:14:01.080 --> 00:14:03.720
Much to the surprise
of the dastardly pair,

00:14:03.720 --> 00:14:06.450
though worried about the
execution of their frame-up,

00:14:06.450 --> 00:14:10.530
they still don't know how
close the police really are.

00:14:10.530 --> 00:14:11.930
Captain Wolfe asked Leopold

00:14:11.930 --> 00:14:13.420
about his neighbor Bobby Franks

00:14:13.420 --> 00:14:16.350
and asked where Leopold saw him last.

00:14:16.350 --> 00:14:19.290
After Wolfe tells Leopold
about Bobby's grim faith,

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:21.420
Leopold offers his flimsy alibi

00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:23.550
and implicated innocent George Lewis,

00:14:23.550 --> 00:14:26.090
saying he's known to
frequent the side of Indiana

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:27.910
where Bobby's body was found.

00:14:27.910 --> 00:14:30.800
Clearly, Leopold hopes
to plant a red herring,

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:32.810
but this bird expert has no way of knowing

00:14:32.810 --> 00:14:34.720
that that fish wouldn't swim.

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:37.220
As soon as the captain
finishes speaking with Leopold,

00:14:37.220 --> 00:14:39.090
Leopold rushes back to Loeb.

00:14:39.090 --> 00:14:40.720
The two immediately drive to a park

00:14:40.720 --> 00:14:42.830
where Loeb hurriedly twist the keys off

00:14:42.830 --> 00:14:45.090
the typewriter used to
type the ransom note.

00:14:45.090 --> 00:14:47.800
They throw the keys and the
typewriter into a lagoon,

00:14:47.800 --> 00:14:49.470
but their efforts are in vain.

00:14:49.470 --> 00:14:51.300
By this point, the
police have already been

00:14:51.300 --> 00:14:52.680
collecting evidence and witnesses

00:14:52.680 --> 00:14:55.530
against the nefarious duo
for the last 10 hours.

00:14:55.530 --> 00:14:59.700
The most damning evidence,
Leopold's forgotten glasses.

00:14:59.700 --> 00:15:03.380
The police follow one clue
after another for six days.

00:15:03.380 --> 00:15:05.680
Identifying the glasses' owner was simple.

00:15:05.680 --> 00:15:07.830
Mr. Coe the owner of an eyewear shop

00:15:07.830 --> 00:15:11.480
immediately recognizes the
glasses as one of a rare design.

00:15:11.480 --> 00:15:14.860
Coe tells the police only
three customers owned that set,

00:15:14.860 --> 00:15:17.700
and one of them is Leopold.

00:15:17.700 --> 00:15:19.480
By May 28th, the police have spent

00:15:19.480 --> 00:15:21.110
almost a week tracking down leads,

00:15:21.110 --> 00:15:23.510
collecting clues, gather tangible proof,

00:15:23.510 --> 00:15:26.340
and creating a long list of eyewitnesses.

00:15:26.340 --> 00:15:28.270
At this point, they
decide it's time to hear

00:15:28.270 --> 00:15:31.460
whatever fantastic story Leopold
and Loeb have come up with.

00:15:31.460 --> 00:15:32.293
The police questioned

00:15:32.293 --> 00:15:34.610
the self-proclaimed geniuses separately,

00:15:34.610 --> 00:15:36.300
hoping to get a confession to support

00:15:36.300 --> 00:15:37.600
the mountain of evidence

00:15:37.600 --> 00:15:39.410
already in the law's possession.

00:15:39.410 --> 00:15:41.620
The questions take place at a local hotel

00:15:41.620 --> 00:15:43.070
in the hopes of making the criminals

00:15:43.070 --> 00:15:45.840
feel more comfortable
and more likely to sing.

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:47.510
Leopold continues to offer the police

00:15:47.510 --> 00:15:49.350
names of other possible suspects.

00:15:49.350 --> 00:15:51.030
He then gives two conflicting answers

00:15:51.030 --> 00:15:53.310
about where his spectacles might be.

00:15:53.310 --> 00:15:54.310
Loeb on the other hand

00:15:54.310 --> 00:15:56.330
tries to claim he doesn't
remember what happened,

00:15:56.330 --> 00:15:59.400
hoping to avoid making any
truly damning mistakes.

00:15:59.400 --> 00:16:02.240
Both give police their
flimsy false alibis,

00:16:02.240 --> 00:16:04.407
but Leopold is too
reckless and even admits,

00:16:04.407 --> 00:16:05.827
"If I were to murder anybody,

00:16:05.827 --> 00:16:07.207
"it would be just such a cocky

00:16:07.207 --> 00:16:09.580
"little son of bitch as Bobby Franks."

00:16:09.580 --> 00:16:12.200
The police released the men for the night,

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:14.750
but secretly had them followed.

00:16:14.750 --> 00:16:18.010
Finally, around 1:00 a.m. on May 30th,

00:16:18.010 --> 00:16:19.560
Leopold and Loeb are arrested

00:16:19.560 --> 00:16:21.770
for the murder of Bobby Franks.

00:16:21.770 --> 00:16:23.810
Once at the station for processing,

00:16:23.810 --> 00:16:25.830
the police give the two some details

00:16:25.830 --> 00:16:28.800
about the mountain of
evidence stacked against them.

00:16:28.800 --> 00:16:32.630
Loeb is the first to break
and start confessing.

00:16:32.630 --> 00:16:36.440
And when Leopold finds
out, he confesses too.

00:16:36.440 --> 00:16:40.210
Finally, the Franks are on
their way to some justice

00:16:40.210 --> 00:16:41.373
for their little boy.

00:16:42.840 --> 00:16:44.840
But it turns out that the path to justice

00:16:44.840 --> 00:16:47.160
is a truly twisted road.

00:16:47.160 --> 00:16:48.510
Leopold and Loeb's families

00:16:48.510 --> 00:16:50.560
hired the most famous lawyer in the world,

00:16:50.560 --> 00:16:54.170
Clarence Darrow of the
Scopes Monkey Trial fame,

00:16:54.170 --> 00:16:57.250
and they pay him a $70,000 retainer,

00:16:57.250 --> 00:16:58.180
which was a fortune

00:16:58.180 --> 00:17:00.700
and would be over a million dollars today.

00:17:00.700 --> 00:17:03.140
Billed as the trial of the century,

00:17:03.140 --> 00:17:04.870
this is in every way the predecessor

00:17:04.870 --> 00:17:06.840
to the OJ Simpson case.

00:17:06.840 --> 00:17:09.810
But given the grizzly facts of the trial,

00:17:09.810 --> 00:17:13.590
why would the most famous lawyer
in the world take the case?

00:17:13.590 --> 00:17:16.820
Because he was staunchly
against the death penalty.

00:17:16.820 --> 00:17:19.100
Darrow famously opposed capital punishment

00:17:19.100 --> 00:17:20.400
throughout his career,

00:17:20.400 --> 00:17:22.330
but the facts are not in dispute.

00:17:22.330 --> 00:17:25.560
Two brilliant young minds
decided to kill a young boy

00:17:25.560 --> 00:17:28.870
just to see if they could
complete the perfect crime.

00:17:28.870 --> 00:17:30.530
The killers confessed.

00:17:30.530 --> 00:17:33.790
Darrow knows that if Leopold
and Loeb plead not guilty,

00:17:33.790 --> 00:17:36.950
they will be convicted by a
jury and sentenced to death.

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:38.650
Even the greatest lawyer in the world

00:17:38.650 --> 00:17:40.203
can only do so much.

00:17:42.140 --> 00:17:44.490
So, Darrow's astute legal mind

00:17:44.490 --> 00:17:47.200
comes up with a tactic that might at least

00:17:47.200 --> 00:17:49.590
save their twisted lives.

00:17:49.590 --> 00:17:51.920
Darrow suggest the pair skip the trial

00:17:51.920 --> 00:17:54.600
and focus exclusively on sentencing.

00:17:54.600 --> 00:17:57.930
On the day of the indictment,
the town is in a tissy,

00:17:57.930 --> 00:17:59.890
and people all over the
country want to know

00:17:59.890 --> 00:18:03.260
how these two calculating
child killers will plead.

00:18:03.260 --> 00:18:06.540
What could they possibly
say to defend themselves?

00:18:06.540 --> 00:18:07.610
Let's go to the courtroom

00:18:07.610 --> 00:18:10.320
where the opposing lawyers
are about to square off.

00:18:10.320 --> 00:18:12.550
In a courtroom jammed with people

00:18:12.550 --> 00:18:14.813
but so silent you could hear a pin drop.

00:18:16.050 --> 00:18:18.950
- [Judge] Mr. Darrow,
how do your client plead

00:18:18.950 --> 00:18:22.610
to the counts of kidnapping
and first degree murder?

00:18:22.610 --> 00:18:23.586
- [Clarence] Guilty.

00:18:23.586 --> 00:18:24.419
(gasps)

00:18:24.419 --> 00:18:27.290
- The courtroom is full of
shock, gasps, and murmurs.

00:18:27.290 --> 00:18:28.700
But once it's quiet again,

00:18:28.700 --> 00:18:31.470
Darrow simply requests a
full hearing on sentencing

00:18:31.470 --> 00:18:34.530
before the court decides
on the killer's penalty.

00:18:34.530 --> 00:18:36.390
The court grants his requests.

00:18:36.390 --> 00:18:38.800
So, in Illinois, is pleading guilty

00:18:38.800 --> 00:18:40.930
enough to avoid the death penalty

00:18:40.930 --> 00:18:43.460
for first degree murder and kidnapping.

00:18:43.460 --> 00:18:45.180
The state's attorney, Robert Crowe,

00:18:45.180 --> 00:18:47.730
is certain that this will be hanging case.

00:18:47.730 --> 00:18:50.350
However, there's the Darrow factor,

00:18:50.350 --> 00:18:51.950
and Darrow is even smarter

00:18:51.950 --> 00:18:54.080
than the two men he's defending.

00:18:54.080 --> 00:18:57.510
Darrow is aware that a plea
of insanity will be futile.

00:18:57.510 --> 00:19:00.160
The facts are known and at
this point in his career,

00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:03.610
the only client that Clarence
Darrow ever lost to execution

00:19:03.610 --> 00:19:06.800
tried the insanity defense
and failed miserably.

00:19:06.800 --> 00:19:10.020
So Darrow takes a different,
more audacious route,

00:19:10.020 --> 00:19:12.260
sending the case into an unbelievable

00:19:12.260 --> 00:19:15.920
32-day hearing on sentencing alone.

00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:17.870
Will Darrow be able to convince the court

00:19:17.870 --> 00:19:20.200
that life sentences are sufficient?

00:19:20.200 --> 00:19:22.740
Or, will these two sociopaths hang

00:19:22.740 --> 00:19:24.700
for their terrible crime?

00:19:24.700 --> 00:19:26.630
Let's see what the Cook County Court

00:19:26.630 --> 00:19:29.790
decided in September of 1924.

00:19:29.790 --> 00:19:31.250
We take you to the courthouse

00:19:31.250 --> 00:19:35.097
where the historic
sentencing is about to begin.

00:19:35.097 --> 00:19:38.303
(typewriter clicking)

00:19:38.303 --> 00:19:39.350
- [Judge] Good morning.

00:19:39.350 --> 00:19:41.530
I'd like to first express that

00:19:41.530 --> 00:19:44.210
while this case has
attracted a lot of attention

00:19:44.210 --> 00:19:45.810
in the community at large,

00:19:45.810 --> 00:19:49.000
I will not allow this
courtroom to become a circus.

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:52.870
We are here only to resolve
the matter of sentencing.

00:19:52.870 --> 00:19:54.640
Is the state ready to proceed?

00:19:54.640 --> 00:19:55.473
- [Robert] Yes, Your Honor.

00:19:55.473 --> 00:19:58.160
Robert Crowe for the people
of the state of Illinois.

00:19:58.160 --> 00:19:59.830
- [Judge] Counsel for defendants?

00:19:59.830 --> 00:20:00.663
- [Clarence] Yes, Judge.

00:20:00.663 --> 00:20:03.190
Clarence Darrow on
behalf of Nathan Leopold

00:20:03.190 --> 00:20:04.480
and Richard Loeb.

00:20:04.480 --> 00:20:05.390
- [Judge] All right then.

00:20:05.390 --> 00:20:07.440
Mr. Crowe, you may begin.

00:20:07.440 --> 00:20:09.450
- [Robert] Thank you, and
may it please the court.

00:20:09.450 --> 00:20:10.970
Your Honor, these defendants

00:20:10.970 --> 00:20:13.900
are nothing less than
depraved hyper sociopath

00:20:13.900 --> 00:20:16.310
who think nothing of human life.

00:20:16.310 --> 00:20:18.880
If ever a case for the
death penalty existed,

00:20:18.880 --> 00:20:20.060
it is this one.

00:20:20.060 --> 00:20:21.790
These man admitted that they planned

00:20:21.790 --> 00:20:24.720
and committed the gruesome
murder of a young boy,

00:20:24.720 --> 00:20:27.540
an innocent child who presented no threat,

00:20:27.540 --> 00:20:30.910
because they thought it
would be a fun experiment.

00:20:30.910 --> 00:20:32.610
Moreover, they both stated

00:20:32.610 --> 00:20:34.900
that this heinous act was thrilling,

00:20:34.900 --> 00:20:36.570
and Mr. Leopold has admitted

00:20:36.570 --> 00:20:38.150
that he had an interesting in learning

00:20:38.150 --> 00:20:41.580
what it would be like
to murder a human being.

00:20:41.580 --> 00:20:42.730
- [Clarence] Objection, Your Honor.

00:20:42.730 --> 00:20:45.400
Counsel is offering
evidence not in the record

00:20:45.400 --> 00:20:47.160
as there was no trial in which my clients

00:20:47.160 --> 00:20:48.680
testified under oath.

00:20:48.680 --> 00:20:50.260
- [Judge] Objection sustained.

00:20:50.260 --> 00:20:51.800
Be careful, Mr. Crowe.

00:20:51.800 --> 00:20:52.870
Proceed.

00:20:52.870 --> 00:20:54.380
- [Robert] Are the defendants sick?

00:20:54.380 --> 00:20:57.440
Yes, but not from any mental illness,

00:20:57.440 --> 00:21:01.080
but instead a knowingly
embraced depravity.

00:21:01.080 --> 00:21:03.400
I hesitate to even call them men,

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:06.320
as true men would never
do or even consider

00:21:06.320 --> 00:21:09.110
such violence toward a poor child.

00:21:09.110 --> 00:21:10.880
I urge the point to consider

00:21:10.880 --> 00:21:14.260
to the endless anguish in
which Bobby's parents will have

00:21:14.260 --> 00:21:16.500
to live the rest of their lives.

00:21:16.500 --> 00:21:20.380
Capital punishment was
made for just such a case.

00:21:20.380 --> 00:21:22.400
- [Judge] Your argument, Mr, Darrow.

00:21:22.400 --> 00:21:23.910
- [Clarence] Your Honor, it has been said

00:21:23.910 --> 00:21:26.020
that we plead guilty because we are afraid

00:21:26.020 --> 00:21:27.240
to do anything else.

00:21:27.240 --> 00:21:28.240
That is true.

00:21:28.240 --> 00:21:31.280
We seek mercy, but not exoneration.

00:21:31.280 --> 00:21:33.690
Now we have said to the
public and to this court

00:21:33.690 --> 00:21:36.270
that neither the parents, nor the friends,

00:21:36.270 --> 00:21:38.170
nor the attorneys of these boys

00:21:38.170 --> 00:21:39.610
would want them released.

00:21:39.610 --> 00:21:42.690
Unfortunate though it may be, it is true,

00:21:42.690 --> 00:21:45.360
and those the closest to
them know perfectly well

00:21:45.360 --> 00:21:46.890
that they would not be released

00:21:46.890 --> 00:21:48.660
and that they should be permanently

00:21:48.660 --> 00:21:50.460
isolated from society.

00:21:50.460 --> 00:21:53.950
We are only asking this
court to save their lives.

00:21:53.950 --> 00:21:56.360
The key question in this case is not

00:21:56.360 --> 00:21:58.950
whether my clients did something horrific,

00:21:58.950 --> 00:22:01.420
but rather whether
there were circumstances

00:22:01.420 --> 00:22:04.550
that mitigate their level
of personal responsibility.

00:22:04.550 --> 00:22:06.070
Despite counsel's attempt

00:22:06.070 --> 00:22:09.110
to paint Nathan and Richard as inhuman,

00:22:09.110 --> 00:22:10.440
they certainly are not.

00:22:10.440 --> 00:22:13.276
They are young men whose minds have been

00:22:13.276 --> 00:22:16.140
are still being molded
by the world around them,

00:22:16.140 --> 00:22:18.110
as well as the smaller environment

00:22:18.110 --> 00:22:20.790
in which they live out
every day of their lives,

00:22:20.790 --> 00:22:23.760
their parents' home,
their college classes,

00:22:23.760 --> 00:22:25.550
their sports practices and the like.

00:22:25.550 --> 00:22:26.960
And these smaller worlds

00:22:26.960 --> 00:22:30.500
which are intimate to my
clients must be closely examined

00:22:30.500 --> 00:22:34.420
before deciding on a fair and
just penalty for their crimes.

00:22:34.420 --> 00:22:36.750
- [Judge] The state may
proceed with argument.

00:22:36.750 --> 00:22:39.210
- [Robert] Over 100
witnesses for the state

00:22:39.210 --> 00:22:41.280
testified to the countless lies,

00:22:41.280 --> 00:22:43.630
attempts to implicate innocent people,

00:22:43.630 --> 00:22:47.840
and path of destruction left
behind by these two ghouls.

00:22:47.840 --> 00:22:51.200
That evidence, combined with
the hard tangible evidence,

00:22:51.200 --> 00:22:54.940
is enough to warrant death for
these abhorrent defendants.

00:22:54.940 --> 00:22:57.120
- [Judge] Mr. Darrow,
did you want to comment

00:22:57.120 --> 00:22:59.010
on witness or evidence.

00:22:59.010 --> 00:23:00.510
- [Clarence] Yes, thank you, Judge.

00:23:00.510 --> 00:23:02.070
As the court has seen,

00:23:02.070 --> 00:23:04.670
we produced many witnesses for the court,

00:23:04.670 --> 00:23:06.920
including psychiatric experts

00:23:06.920 --> 00:23:08.930
and those individuals closest to

00:23:08.930 --> 00:23:12.420
and familiar with the daily
lives of Nathan and Richard.

00:23:12.420 --> 00:23:14.910
Their reliable testimony
and other evidence

00:23:14.910 --> 00:23:18.800
has shown that my clients
are not deserving of death.

00:23:18.800 --> 00:23:21.160
- [Judge] Mr. Crowe,
please advise the court

00:23:21.160 --> 00:23:23.840
of the state's recommendation
for sentencing.

00:23:23.840 --> 00:23:26.010
- [Robert] The state is
recommending death by hanging

00:23:26.010 --> 00:23:27.560
for both of the defendants.

00:23:27.560 --> 00:23:29.790
Leopold and Loeb are highly educated,

00:23:29.790 --> 00:23:31.870
and they were raised by kind and civilized

00:23:31.870 --> 00:23:33.340
members of society,

00:23:33.340 --> 00:23:36.560
therefore they were well
aware that life is value

00:23:36.560 --> 00:23:38.830
and that it is a against the law

00:23:38.830 --> 00:23:42.500
in every state of the union
to murder an innocent person.

00:23:42.500 --> 00:23:45.700
Furthermore, they soberly
planned and brutally executed

00:23:45.700 --> 00:23:48.370
the murder of an innocent 14-year-old boy,

00:23:48.370 --> 00:23:51.690
leaving two parents to
grieve and profoundly suffer

00:23:51.690 --> 00:23:53.580
for the rest of their lives.

00:23:53.580 --> 00:23:57.640
Execution is the only
fair and just sentence.

00:23:57.640 --> 00:23:58.550
Thank you.

00:23:58.550 --> 00:24:02.030
- [Judge] Mr. Darrow, your
position for the record, please.

00:24:02.030 --> 00:24:04.550
- [Clarence] Your Honor,
what is the law of Illinois?

00:24:04.550 --> 00:24:06.430
If one is found guilty of murder

00:24:06.430 --> 00:24:08.300
in the first degree by a jury

00:24:08.300 --> 00:24:10.810
or if he pleads guilty before a court,

00:24:10.810 --> 00:24:14.150
the court or jury may
do one of three things,

00:24:14.150 --> 00:24:16.750
you may hang, you may imprison for life,

00:24:16.750 --> 00:24:20.440
or you may imprison for a term
of not less than 14 years.

00:24:20.440 --> 00:24:22.550
Now, is that the law?

00:24:22.550 --> 00:24:25.090
Does it follow from the
statute that a court

00:24:25.090 --> 00:24:27.680
is bound to ascertain the impossible

00:24:27.680 --> 00:24:30.910
and must necessarily measure
the degrees of guilt?

00:24:30.910 --> 00:24:31.830
Not at all.

00:24:31.830 --> 00:24:33.520
It may not be able to do it.

00:24:33.520 --> 00:24:37.360
A court may act from any
reason or from no reason.

00:24:37.360 --> 00:24:40.210
A jury may fix any one of these penalties

00:24:40.210 --> 00:24:41.510
as they separate.

00:24:41.510 --> 00:24:43.450
The defendants plead for life in prison

00:24:43.450 --> 00:24:44.950
over the death sentence.

00:24:44.950 --> 00:24:46.210
- [Judge] Thank you, Mr. Darrow.

00:24:46.210 --> 00:24:48.270
The state's position is well-known.

00:24:48.270 --> 00:24:51.640
Please proceed with your case
for life rather than death.

00:24:51.640 --> 00:24:53.880
- [Clarence] This terrible crime, Judge,

00:24:53.880 --> 00:24:56.350
was inborn in their very nature,

00:24:56.350 --> 00:24:58.210
handed down from ancestry.

00:24:58.210 --> 00:25:00.260
Could any young student be blamed

00:25:00.260 --> 00:25:02.880
because he took Nietzsche's
philosophy seriously

00:25:02.880 --> 00:25:04.890
and fashioned his life upon them.

00:25:04.890 --> 00:25:08.100
Now, Your Honor, we must
also talk of the great war.

00:25:08.100 --> 00:25:10.390
Before long years, the civilized world

00:25:10.390 --> 00:25:13.120
was engaged in killing
men by the thousands.

00:25:13.120 --> 00:25:14.140
Do you suppose this world

00:25:14.140 --> 00:25:15.750
has ever been the same since?

00:25:15.750 --> 00:25:18.740
We have read of killing
100,000 men in the day.

00:25:18.740 --> 00:25:21.970
These boys were brought
up in such an environment.

00:25:21.970 --> 00:25:24.650
The tales of death were in their homes,

00:25:24.650 --> 00:25:27.070
their playgrounds, their schools.

00:25:27.070 --> 00:25:30.320
They learned to place a
cheap value on human life.

00:25:30.320 --> 00:25:31.940
- [Judge] Mr. Crowe, does the state

00:25:31.940 --> 00:25:34.730
have any evidence to
refute Mr. Darrow's point

00:25:34.730 --> 00:25:37.760
regarding the effects of
war on the minds of children

00:25:37.760 --> 00:25:39.206
and their value of life?

00:25:39.206 --> 00:25:40.510
- [Robert] Of course.

00:25:40.510 --> 00:25:42.880
The state offers simple common sense.

00:25:42.880 --> 00:25:44.430
Look at the thousands of children

00:25:44.430 --> 00:25:46.510
the same age as the defendants

00:25:46.510 --> 00:25:49.250
who also live through
the tragic days of war.

00:25:49.250 --> 00:25:50.800
They haven't killed anyone.

00:25:50.800 --> 00:25:53.870
And if I'm unaware of
one or more who have,

00:25:53.870 --> 00:25:56.970
then it's still evidence
that Mr. Darrow's argument

00:25:56.970 --> 00:25:58.550
does not hold water.

00:25:58.550 --> 00:26:01.250
- [Clarence] Your Honor
knows that in this very court

00:26:01.250 --> 00:26:04.490
crimes of violence have
increased since the war,

00:26:04.490 --> 00:26:06.680
not necessarily by those who fought,

00:26:06.680 --> 00:26:07.710
but by those how learned

00:26:07.710 --> 00:26:10.450
that blood was cheap and
human life was cheap.

00:26:10.450 --> 00:26:12.240
If the state and our country

00:26:12.240 --> 00:26:14.000
could take these lives lightly,

00:26:14.000 --> 00:26:15.690
why not young boys?

00:26:15.690 --> 00:26:18.040
There are causes for this crime.

00:26:18.040 --> 00:26:19.270
War is part of it.

00:26:19.270 --> 00:26:20.920
Education is part of it.

00:26:20.920 --> 00:26:21.960
Birth is part of it.

00:26:21.960 --> 00:26:23.270
Money is part of it.

00:26:23.270 --> 00:26:26.130
All these conspired to encompass

00:26:26.130 --> 00:26:28.570
the destruction of these two poor boys.

00:26:28.570 --> 00:26:30.420
If the welfare of the community

00:26:30.420 --> 00:26:33.100
would be benefited by taking these lives,

00:26:33.100 --> 00:26:34.260
well and good.

00:26:34.260 --> 00:26:36.840
I however think it would
work a greater evil

00:26:36.840 --> 00:26:38.550
that no one could measure.

00:26:38.550 --> 00:26:40.660
All murders have a cause.

00:26:40.660 --> 00:26:43.060
Why did they kill little Bobby Franks?

00:26:43.060 --> 00:26:46.910
They killed him as they
might kill a spider or a fly,

00:26:46.910 --> 00:26:48.740
for the experience.

00:26:48.740 --> 00:26:51.430
They killed him because
they were made that way,

00:26:51.430 --> 00:26:53.810
because somewhere in
the infinite processes

00:26:53.810 --> 00:26:57.300
that go into the making
up of the boy or the man,

00:26:57.300 --> 00:26:58.390
something slipped.

00:26:58.390 --> 00:27:01.920
And those unfortunate
lads sit there hated,

00:27:01.920 --> 00:27:04.120
despised, outcasts,

00:27:04.120 --> 00:27:06.710
with the community
shouting for their blood.

00:27:06.710 --> 00:27:08.510
- [Robert] My I respond to Mr. Darrow's

00:27:08.510 --> 00:27:09.435
last arguments, please?

00:27:09.435 --> 00:27:11.110
- [Judge] Go ahead.

00:27:11.110 --> 00:27:13.300
- [Robert] Without getting
into specific details,

00:27:13.300 --> 00:27:15.990
suffice to say, the
collection of testimony

00:27:15.990 --> 00:27:18.600
from over 100 of the state's witnesses

00:27:18.600 --> 00:27:20.340
is from reliable people

00:27:20.340 --> 00:27:22.530
whose accounts are all consistent

00:27:22.530 --> 00:27:25.210
and most importantly demonstrated coldness

00:27:25.210 --> 00:27:27.930
and even enjoyment on the
part of the defendants

00:27:27.930 --> 00:27:29.770
during every step of their planning,

00:27:29.770 --> 00:27:33.660
execution, and post-murder
deceitful actions.

00:27:33.660 --> 00:27:34.670
- [Judge] Thank you, Mr. Crowe.

00:27:34.670 --> 00:27:37.130
Mr. Darrow, you may continue.

00:27:37.130 --> 00:27:38.370
- [Clarence] I have been sorry,

00:27:38.370 --> 00:27:41.500
and I'm sorry for the bereavement
of Mr. and Mrs. Franks

00:27:41.500 --> 00:27:44.810
for all those broken ties
that cannot be healed.

00:27:44.810 --> 00:27:47.180
All I can hope and wish is that some good

00:27:47.180 --> 00:27:48.450
may come from it all.

00:27:48.450 --> 00:27:50.810
I know the boys are
not fit to be at large.

00:27:50.810 --> 00:27:53.160
The easy thing and the popular thing to do

00:27:53.160 --> 00:27:54.840
would be to hang my clients.

00:27:54.840 --> 00:27:57.350
The cruel and thoughtless will approve.

00:27:57.350 --> 00:27:58.870
- [Judge] Be careful, Mr. Darrow.

00:27:58.870 --> 00:28:02.310
This court does not make
decisions based on what's popular.

00:28:02.310 --> 00:28:05.810
It answers only to the laws on the books.

00:28:05.810 --> 00:28:08.220
- [Clarence] I intended
no disrespect, Your Honor.

00:28:08.220 --> 00:28:11.490
But in Chicago and
reaching over the length

00:28:11.490 --> 00:28:12.880
and breadth of the land,

00:28:12.880 --> 00:28:15.490
more and more fathers and mothers,

00:28:15.490 --> 00:28:18.090
the humane, the kind, the hopeful

00:28:18.090 --> 00:28:21.290
will join in no acclaim at
the death of my clients.

00:28:21.290 --> 00:28:23.880
They would ask that the
shedding of blood be stopped

00:28:23.880 --> 00:28:25.660
and that the normal feelings of men

00:28:25.660 --> 00:28:27.240
resume this way.

00:28:27.240 --> 00:28:30.700
90 poor, unfortunate man
have given up their lives

00:28:30.700 --> 00:28:32.380
to stop murder in Chicago.

00:28:32.380 --> 00:28:35.090
90 men have been hanged
by the neck until dead

00:28:35.090 --> 00:28:37.860
because of the ancient
superstition that in some way

00:28:37.860 --> 00:28:41.270
hanging one man keeps another
from committing a crime,

00:28:41.270 --> 00:28:42.990
and that the only way to treat crime

00:28:42.990 --> 00:28:45.830
is to intimidate everyone into goodness

00:28:45.830 --> 00:28:47.450
and obedience to law.

00:28:47.450 --> 00:28:51.400
I am pleading for life,
understanding, charity,

00:28:51.400 --> 00:28:55.180
kindness, and infinite
mercy that considers all.

00:28:55.180 --> 00:28:58.670
I'm pleading that we overcome
cruelty with kindness,

00:28:58.670 --> 00:29:00.200
and hatred with love.

00:29:00.200 --> 00:29:02.570
And you may hang them by
the neck until they're dead.

00:29:02.570 --> 00:29:06.360
But in doing so, you would
turn your face toward the past.

00:29:06.360 --> 00:29:08.610
In doing it, you would be making it harder

00:29:08.610 --> 00:29:11.660
for every other boy who
in ignorance and darkness

00:29:11.660 --> 00:29:14.070
must grope his way through the mazes

00:29:14.070 --> 00:29:15.960
which only childhood knows.

00:29:15.960 --> 00:29:18.580
If Your Honor can hang a boy at 18,

00:29:18.580 --> 00:29:22.510
some other judge hang
him at 17, or 16, or, 14.

00:29:22.510 --> 00:29:24.740
Someday, if there is any such thing

00:29:24.740 --> 00:29:26.180
as progress in the world,

00:29:26.180 --> 00:29:28.210
if there's any spirit of humanity

00:29:28.210 --> 00:29:30.280
that is working in the hearts of men,

00:29:30.280 --> 00:29:33.910
someday men would look back
on this as a barbarous age

00:29:33.910 --> 00:29:35.770
which deliberately set itself

00:29:35.770 --> 00:29:39.080
in the way of progress,
humanity, and sympathy,

00:29:39.080 --> 00:29:42.260
and committed an unforgivable act.

00:29:42.260 --> 00:29:43.180
- [Judge] Mr. Crowe,

00:29:43.180 --> 00:29:45.540
tell me how death will
better serve society

00:29:45.540 --> 00:29:47.120
than will life in prison.

00:29:47.120 --> 00:29:48.770
- [Robert] As you said yourself, Judge,

00:29:48.770 --> 00:29:51.950
this court must answer
to the laws on the books.

00:29:51.950 --> 00:29:54.160
This case fall squarely under the law,

00:29:54.160 --> 00:29:56.200
which provides for death by hanging.

00:29:56.200 --> 00:29:58.050
We cannot allow the public to believe

00:29:58.050 --> 00:29:59.790
that our laws are meaningless,

00:29:59.790 --> 00:30:02.820
so it's imperative that
this court abides by the law

00:30:02.820 --> 00:30:03.680
to its letter.

00:30:03.680 --> 00:30:05.880
Furthermore, death by hanging will work

00:30:05.880 --> 00:30:07.440
as a logical deterrent.

00:30:07.440 --> 00:30:10.580
Most people who realize that
they could be hanged for murder

00:30:10.580 --> 00:30:13.420
will opt against committing
such a heinous crime.

00:30:13.420 --> 00:30:15.570
Some people may still kill if they know

00:30:15.570 --> 00:30:18.030
they may only spend part
of their life in prison

00:30:18.030 --> 00:30:21.070
with a strong chance of
parole for good behavior.

00:30:21.070 --> 00:30:23.210
For example, when Leopold and Loeb

00:30:23.210 --> 00:30:25.190
murdered little Bobby Franks,

00:30:25.190 --> 00:30:27.060
they breached the social contract

00:30:27.060 --> 00:30:29.260
that binds us all together.

00:30:29.260 --> 00:30:32.050
Their lives were forfeit the
moment they took Bobby's.

00:30:32.050 --> 00:30:34.840
Hanging these men may
not bring Bobby back,

00:30:34.840 --> 00:30:38.270
but retributive justice
demands that they suffer.

00:30:38.270 --> 00:30:40.500
And if their deaths prevent the loss

00:30:40.500 --> 00:30:44.750
of even one innocent life,
it will have been worth it.

00:30:44.750 --> 00:30:47.720
- [Judge] Mr. Darrow, a
brief closing, please.

00:30:47.720 --> 00:30:48.840
- [Clarence] We have placed our faith

00:30:48.840 --> 00:30:50.610
in the hands of this learned court,

00:30:50.610 --> 00:30:52.690
knowing that it would be more mindful

00:30:52.690 --> 00:30:54.460
and considerate than a jury.

00:30:54.460 --> 00:30:56.420
It is my only hope that we may all

00:30:56.420 --> 00:31:01.200
temper justice with mercy and
overcome hatred with love.

00:31:01.200 --> 00:31:02.276
Thank you.

00:31:02.276 --> 00:31:05.330
(typewriter clicking)

00:31:05.330 --> 00:31:06.460
- So what are your thoughts?

00:31:06.460 --> 00:31:09.250
If you were Judge Caverly,
what would you decide?

00:31:09.250 --> 00:31:11.660
Should these brilliant
but depraved young men

00:31:11.660 --> 00:31:14.810
with luxurious but less
than ideal childhoods

00:31:14.810 --> 00:31:16.250
escape the gallows?

00:31:16.250 --> 00:31:18.170
Put your proposed verdict in the comments.

00:31:18.170 --> 00:31:19.978
How do you think it came out?

00:31:19.978 --> 00:31:22.620
(typewriter clicking)

00:31:22.620 --> 00:31:24.710
Clarence Darrow's sentencing argument

00:31:24.710 --> 00:31:26.830
is the stuff of legal legend.

00:31:26.830 --> 00:31:31.130
He went on for over 12
hours and 20,000 words.

00:31:31.130 --> 00:31:33.887
Commentators called it the
greatest speech of his career

00:31:33.887 --> 00:31:35.330
and the most eloquent argument

00:31:35.330 --> 00:31:37.430
against the death penalty every given.

00:31:37.430 --> 00:31:39.440
Judge Caverly handed down his decision

00:31:39.440 --> 00:31:41.800
on September 10th, 1924

00:31:41.800 --> 00:31:45.000
as the entire country
waited with bated breath.

00:31:45.000 --> 00:31:47.850
The sentence for the murder
and kidnapping convictions

00:31:47.850 --> 00:31:50.270
of both Nathan Leopold and Richard Loeb

00:31:50.270 --> 00:31:55.270
was in order of life
imprisonment, plus 99 years.

00:31:56.170 --> 00:31:57.820
They were spared the gallows.

00:31:57.820 --> 00:32:00.570
And what happened to
Leopold and Loeb themselves?

00:32:00.570 --> 00:32:03.500
Well, they went to jail
for a very long time.

00:32:03.500 --> 00:32:07.600
Loeb was killed in jail 12
years later by a fellow inmate.

00:32:07.600 --> 00:32:09.780
Leopold served out the
rest of his sentence

00:32:09.780 --> 00:32:13.210
and was paroled 33 years later in 1958.

00:32:13.210 --> 00:32:14.840
He eventually moved to Puerto Rico

00:32:14.840 --> 00:32:16.790
and studied wildlife and
died of a heart attack

00:32:16.790 --> 00:32:18.410
at the age of 66.

00:32:18.410 --> 00:32:22.060
The mission of this channel
is to demystify the law,

00:32:22.060 --> 00:32:23.330
and that can be hard on you too

00:32:23.330 --> 00:32:26.220
when you're dealing with sensitive
subjects like this video.

00:32:26.220 --> 00:32:28.830
Because the only thing scarier than murder

00:32:28.830 --> 00:32:30.500
is getting demonetized,

00:32:30.500 --> 00:32:32.050
which is why my creator friends and I

00:32:32.050 --> 00:32:33.710
teamed up to build our own platform

00:32:33.710 --> 00:32:35.250
where creates don't have to worry about

00:32:35.250 --> 00:32:37.800
demonetization or the dreaded algorithm.

00:32:37.800 --> 00:32:38.700
It's called Nebula,

00:32:38.700 --> 00:32:41.180
and we're thrilled to be
partnering with Curiosity Stream.

00:32:41.180 --> 00:32:42.620
Nebula is a place where creators

00:32:42.620 --> 00:32:45.080
can do what they do best, create.

00:32:45.080 --> 00:32:46.170
It's a place where we can both

00:32:46.170 --> 00:32:48.020
house our content at free

00:32:48.020 --> 00:32:50.120
and also experiment
with new original series

00:32:50.120 --> 00:32:51.950
that probably wouldn't work on YouTube.

00:32:51.950 --> 00:32:54.810
In fact, if you liked this
episode of The Case Of,

00:32:54.810 --> 00:32:56.560
you can find an extended version

00:32:56.560 --> 00:32:58.870
that I actually can't show on YouTube.

00:32:58.870 --> 00:33:01.720
It's LegalEagle but now
with 10% more murder.

00:33:01.720 --> 00:33:03.210
And when I say that Nebula is built

00:33:03.210 --> 00:33:05.290
by creators for creators, I mean it.

00:33:05.290 --> 00:33:08.480
Nebula features lots of YouTube's
top educational creators,

00:33:08.480 --> 00:33:11.390
like Knowing Better,
Hbomberguy, Real Engineering,

00:33:11.390 --> 00:33:13.630
Tier Zoo, and tons of others.

00:33:13.630 --> 00:33:15.130
We also get to collaborate in ways

00:33:15.130 --> 00:33:16.340
that wouldn't work on YouTube,

00:33:16.340 --> 00:33:18.570
for example, the Nebula-exclusive series

00:33:18.570 --> 00:33:20.040
called working titles where

00:33:20.040 --> 00:33:21.420
every episode a different creator

00:33:21.420 --> 00:33:24.340
breaks down their favorite
TV intro sequence.

